---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
import AuthorityPanel from '@/components/ia/AuthorityPanel.astro';
import JourneyNav from '@/components/ia/JourneyNav.astro';
---

<Layout title="Six-part semantic package" description="The six distinct semantic outputs that each SPDTF 2.0 working group keeps aligned.">
  <PageMeta category="Ontology journey" variant="brand" updated="SPDTF 2.0 development · semantic package" />
  <h1>The six-part semantic package</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Each group agrees six related kinds of content. Together they make one reviewable
    semantic package; they are not one taxonomy and they are not six competing standards.
  </p>
  <AuthorityPanel destination="spdtf-2" />
  <JourneyNav />

  <h2 id="outputs">Six distinct outputs</h2>
  <table>
    <caption>What each output helps a participant review</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Output</th><th scope="col">Question it answers</th><th scope="col">Typical review material</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Business glossary</th><td>What do practitioners mean by each term?</td><td>Definitions, examples, scope notes, synonyms and ownership.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Data dictionary</th><td>What data is recorded, with what expectations?</td><td>Elements, definitions, value expectations, provenance and stewardship.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Taxonomies</th><td>How are concepts organised into broader and narrower meanings?</td><td>Hierarchical organisations of domain concepts.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Controlled vocabularies</th><td>Which governed labels, codes and values may be used?</td><td>Terms, definitions, codes, value sets and release status.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Resources</th><td>What identifiable things and concepts need stable meaning?</td><td>Resources, identifiers, descriptions and provenance.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Relationships</th><td>How do those resources connect, participate and constrain one another?</td><td>Roles, links, cardinality and business constraints.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="how-used">How the package is used</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Practitioners review plain-language definitions and examples.</li>
    <li>Facilitators align terms, values, resources and relationships with evidence and competency questions.</li>
    <li>The package is represented in an ontology and relevant constraints.</li>
    <li>Tested generators publish RDF, JSON Schema, forms, APIs and human-readable pages as projections.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    RDF/OWL, SKOS, SHACL, JSON Schema, forms and documentation are aligned
    representations or projections of the agreement, not independent sources of meaning.
  </p>

  <h2 id="review">Review boundary</h2>
  <p>
    A group can review its six outputs without editing RDF or JSON Schema syntax. Open
    questions, evidence requests and feedback dispositions remain visible beside the
    candidate version. Interoperability reviews the parts that cross context boundaries.
  </p>
  <p><a href="/spdtf-2/ontologies/bounded-contexts">Next: bounded contexts and the common boundary →</a></p>
</Layout>
